 0 0 125-188-188 186-187 0 125 252 0 0-250-125 0 187-188 188 188-125 0 0 250 250 0 0-126 187 188z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div><div class="modebar-group"><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Zoom in" data-attr="zoom" data-val="in" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 875 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m1 787l0-875 875 0 0 875-875 0z m687-500l-187 0 0-187-125 0 0 187-188 0 0 125 188 0 0 187 125 0 0-187 187 0 0-125z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Zoom out" data-attr="zoom" data-val="out" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 875 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m0 788l0-876 875 0 0 876-875 0z m688-500l-500 0 0 125 500 0 0-125z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Autoscale" data-attr="zoom" data-val="auto" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m250 850l-187 0-63 0 0-62 0-188 63 0 0 188 187 0 0 62z m688 0l-188 0 0-62 188 0 0-188 62 0 0 188 0 62-62 0z m-875-938l0 188-63 0 0-188 0-62 63 0 187 0 0 62-187 0z m875 188l0-188-188 0 0-62 188 0 62 0 0 62 0 188-62 0z m-125 188l-1 0-93-94-156 156 156 156 92-93 2 0 0 250-250 0 0-2 93-92-156-156-156 156 94 92 0 2-250 0 0-250 0 0 93 93 157-156-157-156-93 94 0 0 0-250 250 0 0 0-94 93 156 157 156-157-93-93 0 0 250 0 0 250z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div><div class="modebar-group"><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Toggle Spike Lines" data-attr="_cartesianSpikesEnabled" data-val="on" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="M512 409c0-57-46-104-103-104-57 0-104 47-104 104 0 57 47 103 104 103 57 0 103-46 103-103z m-327-39l92 0 0 92-92 0z m-185 0l92 0 0 92-92 0z m370-186l92 0 0 93-92 0z m0-184l92 0 0 92-92 0z" transform="matrix(1.5 0 0 -1.5 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Show closest data on hover" data-attr="hovermode" data-val="closest" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="ne"><svg viewBox="0 0 1500 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m375 725l0 0-375-375 375-374 0-1 1125 0 0 750-1125 0z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn active" data-title="Compare data on hover" data-attr="hovermode" data-val="x" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="ne"><svg viewBox="0 0 1125 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m187 786l0 2-187-188 188-187 0 0 937 0 0 373-938 0z m0-499l0 1-187-188 188-188 0 0 937 0 0 376-938-1z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div><div class="modebar-group"><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Save plot as PNG" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m500 450c-83 0-150-67-150-150 0-83 67-150 150-150 83 0 150 67 150 150 0 83-67 150-150 150z m400 150h-120c-16 0-34 13-39 29l-31 93c-6 15-23 28-40 28h-340c-16 0-34-13-39-28l-31-94c-6-15-23-28-40-28h-120c-55 0-100-45-100-100v-450c0-55 45-100 100-100h800c55 0 100 45 100 100v450c0 55-45 100-100 100z m-400-550c-138 0-250 112-250 250 0 138 112 250 250 250 138 0 250-112 250-250 0-138-112-250-250-250z m365 380c-19 0-35-16-35-35 0-19 16-35 35-35 19 0 35 16 35 35 0 19-16 35-35 35z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Open in dialog (edit layout)" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="M786 296v-267q0-15-11-26t-25-10h-214v214h-143v-214h-214q-15 0-25 10t-11 26v267q0 1 0 2t0 2l321 264 321-264q1-1 1-4z m124 39l-34-41q-5-5-12-6h-2q-7 0-12 3l-386 322-386-322q-7-4-13-4-7 2-12 7l-35 41q-4 5-3 13t6 12l401 334q18 15 42 15t43-15l136-114v109q0 8 5 13t13 5h107q8 0 13-5t5-13v-227l122-102q5-5 6-12t-4-13z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div></div></div><svg class="main-svg" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" width="662.3333333333334" height="347.33333333333337"><g class="hoverlayer"></g></svg></div></div></div></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(470,20)" x="470" y="20" title="codeHTML" width="560" height="868" class="codeHTML" name="codeHTML" rot="0"><foreignObject x="0" y="0" width="560" height="868" style="width: 560px; height: 868px;"><div name="htmlCode" style="zoom: 0.56; height: 1550px; width: 1000px;" code="&lt;div class=&quot;ch&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Full-Wave Bridge Rectifier Fed by a Transformer (Diode Bridge)&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;ch-card&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Circuit Components&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source (V1):&lt;/strong&gt; 50 Hz sine wave, 20 V peak&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Winding resistance (Rp):&lt;/strong&gt; 10 &amp;Omega; in series with the primary. A transformer winding is a short circuit in DC, so a small series resistance is always needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transformer (T1):&lt;/strong&gt; L1 = 100 mH, L2 = 25 mH, M = 49.5 mH (coupling factor k = 0.99)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bridge (B1):&lt;/strong&gt; the &lt;em&gt;Diode Bridge&lt;/em&gt; symbol, a model made of four &lt;em&gt;Diode&lt;/em&gt; sub-models: ac1 = A, ac2 = B, plus = Out, minus = gnd. Inside: D1 A&amp;rarr;Out, D2 B&amp;rarr;Out, D3 gnd&amp;rarr;A, D4 gnd&amp;rarr;B&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Filter (C1):&lt;/strong&gt; 100 &amp;micro;F&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Load (R1):&lt;/strong&gt; 1 k&amp;Omega;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;The Transformer&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-formula&quot;&gt;
$n = \dfrac{N_2}{N_1} = \sqrt{\dfrac{L_2}{L_1}} = \sqrt{\dfrac{25}{100}} = \dfrac{1}{2}$ &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; $V_{2,peak} \approx n\,V_{1,peak} = 0.5 \times 20 = \mathbf{10\ V}$
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The secondary is floating: its terminals A and B are tied to the circuit only through the diodes, which is exactly what the equations of the model need.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;How the Bridge Works&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-grid&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-col blue&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Positive half-cycle (A above B)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B1.D1 and B1.D4 conduct, B1.D2 and B1.D3 are blocked&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Path: A &amp;rarr; D1 &amp;rarr; Out &amp;rarr; R1 and C1 &amp;rarr; gnd &amp;rarr; D4 &amp;rarr; B&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Node A is pulled up to Out + 0.76 V&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Node B is pulled down to gnd &amp;minus; 0.76 V&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-col red&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Negative half-cycle (B above A)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B1.D2 and B1.D3 conduct, B1.D1 and B1.D4 are blocked&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Path: B &amp;rarr; D2 &amp;rarr; Out &amp;rarr; R1 and C1 &amp;rarr; gnd &amp;rarr; D3 &amp;rarr; A&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Node B is pulled up to Out + 0.76 V&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Node A is pulled down to gnd &amp;minus; 0.76 V&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In both half-cycles the current crosses the load in the &lt;strong&gt;same direction&lt;/strong&gt;, so the load sees the absolute value of the secondary voltage minus two diode drops:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-formula&quot;&gt;
$V_{Out} \approx |V_A - V_B| - 2\,V_D \approx 10 - 2 \times 0.76 \approx 8.5\ V$ (first peak)
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;The Filter Capacitor&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;C1 is charged at every peak (twice per period of the source) and supplies the load between the peaks:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-formula&quot;&gt;
$\Delta V \approx \dfrac{I_{load}}{2\,f\,C_1} = \dfrac{7.5\ mA}{2 \times 50 \times 100\ \mu F} \approx \mathbf{0.75\ V}$
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-card&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Simulation (steady state):&lt;/strong&gt; Out varies between about 7.2 V and 7.8 V, a ripple of about 0.6 V at 100 Hz (twice the source frequency)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The formula is an upper bound: the capacitor does not discharge during the whole interval between two peaks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The peak is lower than the first one (8.5 V) because the current taken by C1 at each peak drops voltage in Rp and in the winding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Reading the Plot&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;B&lt;/strong&gt; (secondary): they swing in opposite directions; each one is clamped between about &amp;minus;0.8 V and Out + 0.76 V by the bridge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Out&lt;/strong&gt;: the filtered DC output, with a small ripple at 100 Hz&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Things to Try&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ch-card&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change C1 to 1 mF: the ripple becomes about ten times smaller&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change R1 to 200 &amp;Omega;: the load current grows and so does the ripple&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change L2 to 100 mH and M to 99 mH: the ratio becomes 1:1 and Out rises to about 17 V&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add &lt;em&gt;B1.D1.I&lt;/em&gt; and &lt;em&gt;B1.D3.I&lt;/em&gt; to the outputs of the analysis to see the current of each diode inside the bridge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remove C1: Out follows the rectified wave (pulsating DC)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;ch-card green-border&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Conclusion&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;&quot;&gt;The transformer lowers the 20 V peak to 10 V, the four-diode bridge makes both half-cycles drive the load in the same direction, and C1 smooths the result: about 7.5 V DC with a 0.6 V ripple at twice the line frequency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
"> 
